en:
"Agh!"
"Hold still, damn it."
Shindo clamped his hand over my mouth.{p}

"Then how about licking mine too? It's not fair if Hino's the only one."
It was Fukuzawa.
Fukuzawa took off her shoe and pressed it down on my face.{p}

"...You promised. Give me the ampoule."
"...No."
Right before my eyes, Hino let the ampoule drop to the floor.{p}

"...Ahahaha. Good kid. You've got four hours and thirty minutes left.
As a farewell present, I'll give you my precious wristwatch. Wouldn't want you losing track of time, would we?
Now hurry! Hurry up and drink that antidote!"{p}

I decided to head for the chemistry lab.
There were all kinds of chemicals in there.
I'd heard that the best way to hide something is to put it among things just like it.{p}

I reached the chemistry lab, but...
Damn, I don't have a key!
The key... where's the key★{p}

I hurriedly picked up the receiver.
............No good!
The line's dead.{p}

Day 2.
Grandpa is the same as yesterday.
There was no change worth mentioning.{p}

"Why are you trying to kill me? Answer me."
"To get revenge."
For a moment Kazama smirked, but he quickly remembered his position, put on a pathetic face and said it again.{p}

"...It's for revenge, sir."
"For what?! I don't even know you!
Why would anyone want revenge on me?!"{p}

"Where's the ampoule?"
"No idea. Why don't you look for it yourself?
You can hit me all you like, but isn't that just a waste of time?"{p}

The light was on in the night-duty room.
Yes!
Someone was in there!{p}

"Excuse me! Excuse me! Please! Open the door!"
...There was no answer.
Was the teacher out making the rounds right now?{p}

...Dead!
"Diiiiiie!"
Suddenly, a voice rang out.{p}

On reflex, I hurled the hammer at him.
"Ngh!"
As Shindo threw both hands up in front of his face to block it, I brought down the saw I was holding in my other hand.{p}

"Gyaah!"
The saw bit into Shindo's right hand, and he dropped the knife.
Without stopping, I slammed my body into him, knocked him down and straddled him.{p}

I arrived at the newspaper club room.
I couldn't hear any voices from inside.
Keeping an eye on my surroundings, I went into the club room.{p}

"Gyahh!"
Then, as if possessed, Iwashita drove the chisel into Arai's chest again and again and again.
I could only stand there, dumbstruck, watching it happen.{p}

...There it was.
My name, at the very end.
And written beside it was this...{p}

If I could pry some information out of Kazama, I might find a way through this.
If I kept searching blindly like this, I'd never find the ampoule.
I headed for the art room.{p}

"What's the Murder Club?! Tell me!"
"Eek, please, anything but that. They'll kill me!"
Hosoda started crying again.{p}

"Then you want me to kill you, is that it?
If you don't talk right now, you'll be sorry."
Once I threatened him, Hosoda started blabbing away, even about things I hadn't asked.{p}

What is this guy even saying?
He wants me to join the Murder Club?
...But if I did, I'd be saved.{p}

"What did you say★"
For a moment, I couldn't believe my ears.
"You know where the ampoule is★"{p}

"Trends in Human Life and Death Over One Hundred Days!"
I shouted the report's title at Fukuzawa as she lunged at me.
Suddenly, Fukuzawa froze.{p}

I hurriedly reached up to the ledge of the stall and grabbed the ampoule.
Slowly, so I wouldn't drop it, and so I wouldn't crush it in my grip.
I took the cap off the ampoule and drank it down in one gulp.{p}

...Phew. It looked like I'd made it in time.
Did this mean I was saved?
I'd wait here until the time came.{p}

"...Let's go home. ...I'm going home."
I muttered it over and over to keep my spirits up.
The school gate was right in front of me.{p}

"Ahaha... You can barely even walk.
Me, on the other hand, I'm in perfect shape. There's no need for a contest at all.
Now, die for me. And become the killer who murdered six losers and one teacher."{p}

"Gyah!"
Hino let out a short groan.
Then his eyes rolled back until only the whites showed.{p}

This is one guy I'll never forgive.
I don't care what happens to me!
I clenched my fist and swung at him.{p}

"You bastard... how dare you."
Hino's bloodshot eyes turned on me.
"You're nothing but prey, and you dare do this to me? That settles it. You're sentenced to death, here and now!"{p}

I picked up the receiver.
But when I pressed the buttons, nothing happened.
Right, this one can only receive calls.{p}

I picked up the receiver.
But right away I remembered that the phone line had been cut.
The phone is useless.{p}

I decided to go to the art room.
But I was uneasy.
Would it really be in a place like that?{p}

...The art room door was shut.
Damn it.
Without the key, I can't get in anywhere.{p}

I slammed my shoulder into them.
"Ugh!"
A sharp pain shot through my shoulder.{p}

Oh well.
I loosened my grip a little.
Then Kazama swung his hand up.{p}

After thinking it over and over, this really was the only way.
I let go of Kazama.
"Please, go. I have no intention of hurting you."{p}

Kazama was still beating me.
But I couldn't even feel the pain anymore.
I sank into true darkness.{p}

Someone sent the bed flying with a yell.
Was that voice Hosoda's★
Before I could even check, the hard metal-frame bed slammed into me.{p}

I punched Hosoda hard.
He let out a sob and fell to the floor.
He didn't seem to have any fight left in him.{p}

...But the gym doors were shut tight.
Oh, come on, what am I doing?
I did the exact same thing a minute ago!{p}

I decided to go to the old school building.
I don't have much time left.
I have to hurry.{p}

I went up to the window.
Hardly any glass was left in the frame.
Someone had really gone to town smashing it.{p}

I peered down from the window.
Just then, a chill ran down my back.
Was someone watching me★{p}

...Surely it couldn't be inside this toilet bowl, could it?
I searched it thoroughly.
...Nothing.{p}

...Surely it couldn't be inside this toilet bowl, could it?
I searched it thoroughly.
...Nothing.{p}

Fukuzawa watched me as I fell.
She wore an almost entranced expression.
And that was the last sight I ever saw.{p}

I took the blow full on.
"Ugh!"
For an instant, my vision blurred.{p}

In that moment, Fukuzawa snatched up the ampoule.
"Too bad for you."
With that and a smug smile, Fukuzawa crushed the ampoule in her fist.{p}

For now, I just ran.
With the ampoule in my hands, I had no more business in a place like this.
But Fukuzawa quickly stuck out her foot, and I tripped over it.{p}

A wave of heat, a crackling sound.
Fire!
I hurriedly dashed out of the restroom.{p}

All or nothing!
I slipped right past Kazama.
Apparently even he hadn't expected me to charge straight at him.{p}

"Wh... why, you!"
A faint pain ran across my back.
Checking as I ran, I found the back of my shirt sliced clean open.{p}

Kazama had a blade.
"Wait! Prey isn't allowed to get away!"
Kazama shouted as he chased after me.{p}

"...Let's go home. ...Let's go back home."
I muttered it over and over to keep my spirits up.
The school gate was right in front of me.{p}

...And then.
There they stood, in front of the school gate.
That's right: Hino and Kazama.{p}

"Ngh!"
Kazama's face twisted in pain.
But the next instant...{p}

Kazama drove his knee up into my stomach.
"Ugh!"
As I doubled over, the next blow caught me in the temple.{p}

"Kazama, why do we have to fight each other★"
I shouted.
"Even if you take me down, there's no guarantee Hino will give you the ampoule☆"{p}

"Don't be stupid. You're useless."
Hino said it coldly and kicked Kazama's hand away.
"Even if I gave you the ampoule, with that wound, you're going to die anyway."{p}

On the hate-filled stare of Kazama, who had staggered to his feet.
In his hand he gripped the bloody ice pick he'd pulled from his chest.
"Hino...!"{p}

Hino crashed hard to the ground.
The ice pick sticking out of his back seemed to have taken his life in a single blow.
Kazama dragged himself along the ground toward Hino.{p}

"...There it is, the ampoule..."
Kazama pulled the antidote ampoule from Hino's pocket.
Then he drained its contents in one gulp.{p}

I see...
So it really was over.
The long, long night was finally over.{p}

I hurriedly picked up the receiver.
...No good.
That's right, I'd already found out earlier that the phone line was cut.{p}

The light was on in the night-duty room.
Yes!
Someone was in there!{p}

Shindo staggered and dropped the knife.
Now!
I shoved Shindo down and straddled him.{p}

Shindo was a different kind of person from me.
I had no confidence I could win if I made an enemy of him.
Slowly, I lowered the arms I'd raised to fight.{p}

"All right. Please make me your lackey."
I nodded meekly.
My life matters more than some stupid pride.{p}

In that instant, a jolt ran through the back of my neck.
Shindo had slashed me with the knife.
Why...?{p}

When I tried to open the door, I realized it was locked.
That's right, I have to find the keys.
Without the keys, I can't get in anywhere.{p}

...There it was.
My name, at the very end.
And written beside it was this...{p}

I swung the knife around wildly.
"Gah!"
Someone screamed.{p}

"Why are you trying to kill me?!"
I asked.
I couldn't think of anything I'd done to make someone I'd just met hate me that much.{p}

With a ripping slash, my back was cut open.
Damn it!
There was another one hiding...{p}

"Once you're dead, I get to keep your body. That's the deal.
I'll take such good care of it... Heh heh."
As my consciousness faded, an image of Iwashita hugging my corpse flickered up and vanished.{p}

But Iwashita just grinned.
"You can't kill me. Because I'm in love with you."
...What the hell is she talking about★{p}

When I tried to open the door, I realized it was locked.
That's right, I have to find the keys.
Without the keys, I can't get in anywhere.{p}

Hino licked the bloody knife with a flick of his tongue.
"When you keep on killing, you gradually start to feel like a god.
So just imagine their faces when they're forced to realize they were nothing but worthless people after all."{p}

Hino grinned.
"Huh, that's a sudden change of attitude. Are you plotting something?"
"N-no, I'm not. I just can't take any more. I'll do anything, so please forgive me."{p}

"Looks like you mean it. Get up."
Hino pulled me to my feet.
"In that case, I'll accept you as a fellow member of the Murder Club. Drink this."{p}
